# text = Within this moat there was , as I have said , the fish-pond -- a sheet of water that extended the whole length of the garden and bordering which there was an avenue called the lime-tree walk ; an avenue so shaded from the sun and sky , so screened from observation by the thick shelter of the over-arching trees that it seemed a chosen place for secret meetings or for stolen interviews ; a place in which a conspiracy might have been planned , or a lover's vow registered with equal safety ; and yet it was scarcely twenty paces from the house .
