# text = Often in the cool of the evening Sir Michael Audley would stroll up and down smoking his cigar , with his dogs at his heels , and his pretty young wife dawdling by his side ; but in about ten minutes the baronet and his companion would grow tired of the rustling limes and the still water , hidden under the spreading leaves of the water-lilies , and the long green vista with the broken well at the end , and would stroll back to the drawing-room , where my lady played dreamy melodies by Beethoven and Mendelssohn till her husband fell asleep in his easy-chair .
