# text = For seventeen years he had been a widower with an only child , a daughter , Alicia Audley , now eighteen , and by no means too well pleased at having a step-mother brought home to the Court ; for Miss Alicia had reigned supreme in her father's house since her earliest childhood , and had carried the keys , and jingled them in the pockets of her silk aprons , and lost them in the shrubbery , and dropped them into the pond , and given all manner of trouble about them from the hour in which she entered her teens , and had , on that account , deluded herself into the sincere belief , that for the whole of that period , she had been keeping the house .
