# text = But _this_ was love -- this fever , this longing , this restless , uncertain , miserable hesitation ; these cruel fears that his age was an insurmountable barrier to his happiness ; this sick hatred of his white beard ; this frenzied wish to be young again , with glistening raven hair , and a slim waist , such as he had twenty years before ; these , wakeful nights and melancholy days , so gloriously brightened if he chanced to catch a glimpse of her sweet face behind the window curtains , as he drove past the surgeon's house ; all these signs gave token of the truth , and told only too plainly that , at the sober age of fifty-five , Sir Michael Audley had fallen ill of the terrible fever called love .
