# text = The young man stared about him , open-mouthed and open-eyed he said said Phoebe , glancing at the panels of the octagonal chamber , which were hung with Claudes and Poussins , Wouvermans and Cuyps She lifted a heavy green cloth curtain which hung across a doorway , and led the astonished countryman into a fairy-like boudoir , and thence to a dressing-room , in which the open doors of a wardrobe and a heap of dresses flung about a sofa showed that it still remained exactly as its occupants had left it Her cousin looked around in gawky embarrassment , bewildered by the splendor of the room ; and after some deliberation selected the most substantial of the chairs , on the extreme edge of which he carefully seated himself said the girl cried Luke , staring at the massive walnut-wood and brass inlaid casket answered Phoebe , busy as she spoke in folding the rustling silk dresses , and laying them one by one upon the shelves of the wardrobe .
