# text = So that when , one fine spring morning , about three months before the time of which I am writing , the postman brought him the wedding cards of Sir Michael and Lady Audley , together with a very indignant letter from his cousin , setting forth how her father had just married a wax-dollish young person , no older than Alicia herself , with flaxen ringlets , and a perpetual giggle ; for I am sorry to say that Miss Audley's animus caused her thus to describe that pretty musical laugh which had been so much admired in the late Miss Lucy Graham -- when , I say , these documents reached Robert Audley -- they elicited neither vexation nor astonishment in the lymphatic nature of that gentleman .
