# text = The young man did not answer , but looked slowly round the room , and then at his friend's grave face he said George passed his hand once or twice across his forehead , and then , in a hesitating manner , said , quietly cried George , impatiently , raising himself upon the bed , and staring about him with hollow eyes said Robert Audley , laying his hand gently upon the young man's arm he cried He shook off Robert's restraining hand , and rising from the bed , walked straight to the door exclaimed his friend Robert led him back to the bed , and gently forced him to lie down again .
