# text = Alicia sat with her back to the horses , and he could perceive , even in the dusk , that she was a handsome brunette ; but Lady Audley was seated on the side of the carriage furthest from the inn , and he could see nothing of the fair-haired paragon of whom he had heard so much exclaimed Sir Michael , as his nephew emerged from the inn said the young man , as the baronet shook him by the hand in his own hearty fashion cried Alicia said her cousin Now , so complete was the dominion which Lady Audley had , in her own childish , unthinking way , obtained over her devoted husband , that it was very rarely that the baronet's eyes were long removed from his wife's pretty face .
