# text = The young lady was very much surprised and disappointed at hearing her cousin's determination , and for that very reason pretended to take the matter with supreme indifference she said , carelessly murmured Robert , interrupting his cousin stammered George said Robert said Alicia Miss Audley took a letter from the pocket of her riding-jacket as she spoke -- a pretty , fairy-like note , written on shining paper of a peculiar creamy hue said Robert , as his cousin folded the note She put the letter into his hand , and he contemplated it lazily for a few minutes , while Alicia patted the graceful neck of her chestnut mare , which was anxious to be off once more But absent-minded and gloomy George Talboys had strolled away along the margin of the ditch , and stood striking the bulrushes with his cane , half a dozen paces away from Robert and Alicia said the young lady , impatiently ; for she by no means relished this long disquisition upon my lady's note
