# text = He wished his relations good-night and good-by at about half past ten o'clock ; he should run up to London by the first train to look for George in Figtree Court he said asked my lady Robert Audley felt very low-spirited as he walked slowly home between the shadowy meadows ; more low-spirited still when he re-entered the sitting room at Sun Inn , where he and George had lounged together , staring out of the window and smoking their cigars he said , meditatively With Mr . Audley's lymphatic nature , determination was so much the exception rather than the rule , that when he did for once in his life resolve upon any course of action , he had a certain dogged , iron-like obstinacy that pushed him on to the fulfillment of his purpose .
