# text = The young barrister had brought a couple of dogs with him ; and the country gentleman who gave fifty pounds for a pointer ; and traveled a couple of hundred miles to look at a leash of setters before be struck a bargain , laughed aloud at the two miserable curs , one of which had followed Robert Audley through Chancery Lane , and half the length of Holborn ; while his companion had been taken by the barrister _vi et armis_ from a coster-monger who was ill-using him .
