# text = Lady Audley received her nephew's attentions in that graceful half-childish fashion which her admirers found so charming ; but Alicia was indignant at the change in her cousin's conduct said the young lady , contemptuously , as she bounced into the drawing-room in her riding-habit , after a hunting breakfast , from which Robert had absented himself , preferring a cup of tea in my lady's boudoir said the young man imploringly Miss Audley gave her head a little scornful toss she said , impatiently Mr . Robert Audley opened his handsome gray eyes to their widest extent at this tirade , and looked helplessly at Miss Alicia .
