# text = In order to tell this story to better advantage , the young man left his chair , and , crossing the room , took up his place opposite to Lady Audley , in the embrasure of the window asked my lady , after a pause he answered cried my lady , piteously answered the young man , gravely exclaimed my lady continued the young man , as if he scarcely heard Lady Audley's interruption Faint shadows of green and crimson fell upon my lady's face from the painted escutcheons in the mullioned window by which she sat ; but every trace of the natural color of that face had faded out , leaving it a ghastly ashen gray .
