# text = Robert had picked up the ugliest and leanest of his attendant curs , and was placidly stroking the animal's ears asked Miss Audley , meekly replied her cousin , after considerable deliberation said Miss Audley , crimsoning with bright , indignant blushes up to the roots of her waving brown hair Robert pulled the dog's ears thoughtfully for some moments he said , after a pause exclaimed Alicia ; and opening the door with a violence that made her cousin shiver , she bounced out of the drawing-room Robert called after her ; and , then , as he sunk into an easy-chair , he murmured thoughtfully So poor Sir Harry Towers rode away from Audley Court , looking very crestfallen and dismal .
