# text = The wind came whistling up across the frosty open country , and through the leafless woods , and rattled fiercely at the window-frames murmured Robert He poked the fire , patted his dogs , put on his great coat , rolled a rickety old sofa close to the hearth , wrapped his legs in his railway rug , and stretching himself at full length upon the narrow horsehair cushion , smoked his pipe , and watched the bluish-gray wreaths curling upward to the dingy ceiling he murmured , again I have said that the bar-parlor was only separated from the sitting-room occupied by Robert by a lath-and-plaster partition .
