# text = She smiled as she courtesied to Mr . Robert Audley , and her smile , which laid bare the greater part of this set of square , hungry-looking teeth , by no means added to the beauty of her personal appearance she said , with insinuating civility She was interrupted by little George Talboys , who scrambled down from the high chair upon which he had been perched , and ran to Robert Audley he said Robert Audley took the boy in his arms , and carried him to a little table in the window he said He turned the boy's face to the light , and pushed the brown curls off his forehead with both hands he said the boy answered , eagerly the woman answered , looking rather uneasily at Mr . Robert Audley thought Robert as he turned from the boy to the fair-haired widow , who was edging herself slowly toward the table upon which little George Talboys stood talking to his guardian Mrs .
