# text = Heaven only knows how bitterly this hard man may have felt the separation between himself and his only son , or how much the more terrible the anguish might have been made by that unflinching self-conceit which concealed the torture Mr . Talboys would answer to any one who had the temerity to speak to him about George I believe that Harcourt Talboys hugged himself upon the gloomy Roman grandeur of this speech , and that he would like to have worn a toga , and wrapped himself sternly in its folds , as he turned his back upon poor George's intercessor .
