# text = Madhouses are large and only too numerous ; yet surely it is strange they are not larger , when we think of how many helpless wretches must beat their brains against this hopeless persistency of the orderly outward world , as compared with the storm and tempest , the riot and confusion within -- when we remember how many minds must tremble upon the narrow boundary between reason and unreason , mad to-day and sane to-morrow , mad yesterday and sane to-day .
