# text = The lime-walk seemed like some cloister in this uncertain light cried my lady , peevishly asked Robert , gravely exclaimed Lady Audley answered Robert she answered , with a little laugh Robert Audley heard my lady's quickened breathing , he fancied he could almost hear the loud beating of her heart as she walked by his side , shivering now and then , and with her sable cloak wrapped tightly around her she cried suddenly , after a pause of some moments answered Lady Audley asked Robert cried Lady Audley answered Robert , resolutely replied my lady , carelessly Robert began , gravely said my lady , quickly she added , more deliberately Robert Audley did not notice this observation he repeated said my lady Robert answered , quietly Lady Audley shrugged her shoulders she said continued Robert , without replying to my lady's last observation said my lady asked my lady said Robert asked my lady , eagerly My lady shrugged her graceful shoulders , and flashed bright defiance out of her blue eyes she said cried my lady , her voice rising to that shrill and piercing tone peculiar to her when affected by any intense agitation answered Robert replied my lady carelessly answered my lady said Robert
