# text = He knew enough to know that Sir Michael Audley went away with the barbed arrow , which his nephew's hand had sent home to its aim , rankling in his tortured heart ; he knew that this strange and icy calm was the first numbness of a heart stricken by grief so unexpected as for a time to be rendered almost incomprehensible by a blank stupor of astonishment ; he knew that when this dull quiet had passed away , when little by little , and one by one , each horrible feature of the sufferer's sorrow became first dimly apparent and then terribly familiar to him , the storm would burst in fatal fury , and tempests of tears and cruel thunder-claps of agony would rend that generous heart .
