# text = She hated herself and her beauty she cried She was silent for a little while , but she held her place by the door , as if determined to detain Robert as long as it was her pleasure to do so she said , presently Robert started as she mentioned the name of his lost friend ; his face turned pale in the dusky light , and his breathing grew quicker and louder continued my lady Robert Audley flung his hands and clasped them above his head , with one loud cry of horror he said , after a dreadful pause resumed my lady , in the same hard , dogged tone as that in which she had confessed the wicked story of her life She paused , as if she had expected Robert to speak ; but he stood silent and motionless , waiting for the end she said , petulantly Robert Audley uttered a word of horror when the story was finished .
