# text = The shadow of George Talboys pursued him , even in the comfortable first-class carriage , and was behind him when he looked out of the window , and was yet far ahead of him and the rushing engine , in that thicket toward which the train was speeding , by the side of the unhallowed hiding-place in which the mortal remains of the dead man lay , neglected and uncared for Robert thought , as the chill wind swept across the flat landscape , and struck him with such frozen breath as might have emanated from the lips of the dead He was glad when the train stopped at Brentwood at a few minutes after twelve .
