# text = " With that the surgeon goes to fetch the envelopes , and the young chap takes a pocket-book out of his coat pocket with his left hand ; the cover was wet and dirty , but the inside was clean enough , and he tears out a couple of leaves and begins to write upon 'em as you see ; and he writes dreadful awk'ard with his left hand , and he writes slow , but he contrives to finish what you see , and then he puts the two bits o ' writin ' into the envelopes as the surgeon brings him , and he seals 'em up , and he puts a pencil cross upon one of 'em , and nothing on the other : and then he pays the surgeon for his trouble , and the surgeon says , ain't there nothin ' more he can do for him , and can't he persuade him to stay in Brentwood till his arm's better ; but he says no , no , it ain't possible ; and then he says to me , ' Come along o ' me to the railway station , and I'll give you what I've promised Luke added , parenthetically cried Robert Luke Marks had finished his story , and lay quietly enough , exhausted by having talked so long .
